Portions derived from rawmakase
-------------------------------
The Star-Tetrix lifting steps, the 5/3 wavelet and the transfer curve in
crates/core/src/frame.rs (and their GPU versions in crates/core/src/gpu/) follow the Nikon
HE / HE* decoder of rawmakase (https://github.com/pch/rawmakase):

  Copyright (c) 2026 RAWmakase contributors
  Licensed under the MIT License; the full license text is in LICENSES/rawmakase-MIT.txt.

FFmpeg (macOS desktop app only)
-------------------------------
The macOS desktop app bundles an unmodified static FFmpeg 9.0.2 executable
(Contents/Resources/ffmpeg) from https://www.martin-riedl.de, used as a separate program
to encode Develop exports. FFmpeg is Copyright (c) 2000-2026 the FFmpeg developers and
this build, which includes libx265, is licensed under the GNU General Public License
(https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html). It is not linked into Blue Compressor.
The complete corresponding source code is available at https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-9.0.2.tar.xz
and the build scripts at https://ffmpeg.martin-riedl.de. On written request to the
project (https://github.com/redn3/blue-compressor/issues) we will also provide that
source for at least three years after we last distribute this build.

